  "next_id": 83,
  "notes": [
    {
      "at": [
        -90,
        -32
      ],
      "id": 82,
      "text": "Three chips on I2C1 of the Blue Pill (PB6 SCL, PB7 SDA, 100 kHz) with 4.7 kOhm pull-ups to 3.3 V; their\nA0-A2 pins on GND give the addresses 0x50 (24C02 EEPROM), 0x48 (LM75 sensor) and 0x20 (PCF8574\nexpander). Run (F5) and open Analyzer > UART: the EEPROM stores and reads back a word, the LM75 reports\n23.5 C (change it in its properties), and each push button on P4-P7 lights the LED on P0-P3. Remove a\npull-up resistor to see what happens."
    }
  ],
